Rule 1 (order n must be nonnegative)
{v_1 : int} |= v_1 ≥ 0
>>
Rule 2 (input must not be ComplexDouble to avoid unsupported dtype)
{v_2 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_2) ≠ 10
>>
Rule 3 (if out is provided, its shape must match input)
{v_2 : tensor, v_3 : tensor} |= ndim(v_2) = ndim(v_3) ∧ if ndim(v_2) = 0 then true else ∀ i ∈ [0, ndim(v_2) - 1] : shape(v_2, i) = shape(v_3, i)
>>
Rule 4 (out, if provided, must be floating and match input’s floating dtype)
{v_2 : tensor, v_3 : tensor} |= 6 ≤ dtype_(v_3) ∧ dtype_(v_3) ≤ 8 ∧ if 6 ≤ dtype_(v_2) ∧ dtype_(v_2) ≤ 8 then dtype_(v_3) = dtype_(v_2)
